# W043: structural overlap warning fires when user code re-declares an instance the prelude already defines.
# The prelude seeds EquatableInt via seed_infer_state_from_prelude_cache. Declaring another
# Equatable Int instance triggers check_structural_overlap → W043 warning.
[
  MyEqInt: [instance Equatable
    [pattern [Int]]:
      eq: [fn [let x y] [= x y]]]

  result: true
]

---

%.result
=== out
Bool(true)

=== warn
overlapping instances for class 'Equatable'
